# Release-signing configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to "keystore.properties" (which is gitignored) and fill in
# your real values. Never commit keystore.properties or the .jks keystore —
# they contain the private signing material for your release builds.
#
#   cp keystore.properties.example keystore.properties
#
# Then build a signed release APK with:
#
#   ./gradlew assembleRelease
#
# Absolute path to your release keystore (.jks). Generate one with:
#   keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore release.jks -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 \
#           -validity 10000 -alias fastpay
#
# The continuous-delivery workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml) does not read
# this file: it materialises the same four keys from repository secrets
# (FASTPAY_KEYSTORE_BASE64 / FASTPAY_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD / FASTPAY_KEY_ALIAS /
# FASTPAY_KEY_PASSWORD) into a temporary file at build time, so signing material
# never has to be committed. See that workflow for how to encode the keystore.
#
# Keep the keystore itself somewhere durable and backed up. If you lose it you
# cannot ship an update that upgrades an existing install — Android refuses
# updates signed by a different key.
storeFile=/absolute/path/to/release.jks
storePassword=your-keystore-password
keyAlias=fastpay
keyPassword=your-key-password
